	<key>readme</key>
	<string>Type `fff` in Alfred to search files and directories from the front Finder folder.

Usage: fff &lt;keyword&gt; [depth|-] [up]

1. keyword (required): one word. Start with ^ for a stricter (exact) match.
2. depth (optional): a number, or - to keep the default --max-depth.
3. up (optional): a number of dirs to go up from the Finder dir. 0 means ~.

Examples:
- fff config          match "config", default depth
- fff ^config         exact match
- fff config 3        depth 3
- fff config 3 2      depth 3, from 2 dirs up
- fff config - 0      default depth, from ~</string>
